                                        <article class="dics-module-card">
                                            <div class="dics-module-icon">💬</div>
                                            <h3>Messaging</h3>
                                            <p>WhatsApp Business API, Twilio, SendGrid, custom SMS gateways</p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-module-card">
                                            <div class="dics-module-icon">🏦</div>
                                            <h3>Banking</h3>
                                            <p>Bank statement import, NEFT/RTGS feeds, reconciliation automation</p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-module-card">
                                            <div class="dics-module-icon">📊</div>
                                            <h3>Analytics &amp; BI</h3>
                                            <p>Power BI, Tableau, Metabase, Google Data Studio via Odoo data feeds</p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-module-card">
                                            <div class="dics-module-icon">🤖</div>
                                            <h3>AI &amp; Automation</h3>
                                            <p>Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, Zapier, Make (Integromat), custom AI pipelines
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-module-card dics-module-card-accent">
                                            <div class="dics-module-icon">⚙️</div>
                                            <h3>Enterprise ERP</h3>
                                            <p>SAP, Tally, QuickBooks, Zoho, MS Dynamics — migration and live sync</p>
                                        </article>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </section>

                            <section class="dics-section dics-section-light">
                                <div class="dics-container">
                                    <div class="dics-section-heading">
                                        <div>
                                            <span class="dics-eyebrow">Our Process</span>
                                            <h2>How an integration actually gets built.</h2>
                                        </div>
                                        <p>Four stages, no surprises halfway through.</p>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="dics-process-grid">
                                        <article class="dics-process-card">
                                            <strong>01</strong>
                                            <h3>System Audit &amp; Data Mapping</h3>
                                            <p>We map every data entity, field mapping, transformation rule, and failure
                                                mode before writing a line of code.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-process-card">
                                            <strong>02</strong>
                                            <h3>Architecture &amp; Protocol Design</h3>
                                            <p>Choosing the right protocol, authentication strategy, retry policy, and
                                                error-handling approach for the systems involved.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-process-card">
                                            <strong>03</strong>
                                            <h3>Build &amp; Edge-Case Testing</h3>
                                            <p>Integration built and tested against real data — including failure cases,
                                                timeouts, retries, and rollback scenarios.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-process-card">
                                            <strong>04</strong>
                                            <h3>Production Deployment &amp; Monitoring</h3>
                                            <p>Controlled go-live with monitoring, alerting, and a clear runbook for
                                                handling pipeline failures.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article class="dics-process-card">
                                            <strong>05</strong>
                                            <h3>Documentation &amp; Handoff</h3>
                                            <p>Full technical documentation of every endpoint, field mapping, and
                                                failure handling — owned by you, not locked to us.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </section>

                            <section class="dics-detail-section dics-detail-section--dark">
                                <div class="dics-container">
                                    <div class="dics-detail-section-head dics-detail-section-head--center">
                                        <span class="dics-eyebrow">Why DataInteger</span>
                                        <h2>An integration partner, not a connector plugin.</h2>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="dics-detail-why-grid">
                                        <article>
                                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">precision_manufacturing</span>
                                            <h3>Odoo-native, not bolted on</h3>
                                            <p>
                                                We build integrations that use Odoo's ORM, business logic, and access
                                                controls
                                                directly — not middleware that bypasses your ERP and creates a second
                                                source of truth.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article>
                                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">history</span>
                                            <h3>We've seen these failure modes before</h3>
                                            <p>
                                                Duplicate records, partial syncs, timezone mismatches, API rate limits —
                                                we've hit them all in production and designed our patterns around
                                                avoiding them.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                        <article>
                                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">description</span>
                                            <h3>You own what we build</h3>
                                            <p>
                                                Full source code, complete documentation, and a handoff designed so
                                                your own developers — or any competent Odoo partner — can maintain and
                                                extend the integration without coming back to us.
                                            </p>
                                        </article>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </section>

                            <section class="dics-section dics-section-light">
                                <div class="dics-container">
                                    <div class="dics-centered-heading">
                                        <span class="dics-eyebrow">FAQ</span>
                                        <h2>Common Integration Questions</h2>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="dics-faq-container" style="margin: 0 auto;">
                                        <div class="dics-faq-list">

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>Can you integrate with a system that has no public API?</span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>Sometimes. If the system has a database we can access, a file
                                                        export, or a legacy EDI/FTP interface, we can build around it.
                                                        We'll assess feasibility before scoping.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>How do you handle API rate limits from third-party
                                                        platforms?
                                                    </span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>We design integrations with rate limit awareness from the start —
                                                        request queuing, exponential backoff, and batch calls where the
                                                        API supports it. This is engineered in, not patched in later.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>What happens if a sync fails midway?</span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>Failed sync events are logged with context, queued for retry, and
                                                        — for critical failures — trigger an alert. Partial writes are
                                                        rolled back where possible so your data stays consistent.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>Can the integration handle historical data migration as well
                                                        as live sync?
                                                    </span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>Yes. We typically run a one-time historical migration first, then
                                                        switch to live sync at cutover. The migration and sync logic
                                                        often share the same transformation layer to keep the codebases
                                                        consistent.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>Will the integration survive an Odoo version upgrade?</span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>We build integrations as standard Odoo modules following
                                                        upgrade-conscious practices. When you upgrade Odoo, the
                                                        integration module requires the same upgrade process as any
                                                        other custom module — not a full rebuild.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                            <div class="dics-faq-item">
                                                <button type="button">
                                                    <span>How long does a typical integration project take?</span>
                                                    <b>+</b>
                                                </button>
                                                <div class="dics-faq-answer">
                                                    <p>A single focused integration (e.g. Shopify ↔ Odoo or a payment
                                                        gateway) typically takes 3–6 weeks from requirements to
                                                        production. Multi-system orchestration projects are scoped in
                                                        phases.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </section>

                            <section class="dics-contact-section">
